    "title": "Students' belongings X-rayed after bomb threat at Merced school - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Miranda Adams ,\n4 hours ago\nMERCED, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – Hundreds of students had their belongings X-rayed after a bomb threat at a Merced school Thursday afternoon.\nPolice say the threat targeted Merced High School and involved a vehicle in a school parking lot.\nThe campus was placed on lockdown while officers investigated. Officials say the investigation required clearing the area where the initial threat was reported, conducting a perimeter search of the campus, and examining backpacks with X-ray equipment.\nStudents were then released in small groups.\nAt the time of publication, the threat was not substantiated.\nNo further information about the incident was released.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to YourCentralValley.com | CBS47 and KSEE24.",
